TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (Gadd) and add the 5th note as needed.

TIP:  The music is virtually identical between the two versions with just slight variations in rhythm.  The one here is based on Fogerty’s version.  Pat has a brief choral intro and just one chorus at the end.

TIP:  The recurring (Gadd) (Gadd) - (Em) voicing at the end of the line comes right after the leading (G) of the last word so transition smoothly through that (G) to the first (Gadd).

TIP:  Remember to back off the capo to give you room for the (B7).
  
   
